.TH RWH "1" "Aug 2026" "rwh 0.13.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rwh \- manual page for rwh 0.13.0
.SH DESCRIPTION
rwh 0.12.0
.SS "USAGE:"
.IP
rwh [OPTIONS] <SUBCOMMAND>
.SS "OPTIONS:"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable logging to stdout, for debugging purposes
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SS "SUBCOMMANDS:"
.TP
forward
Forward ports from one machine to another
.TP
receive
Receive a file/folder [alias: rx]
.TP
send
Send a file/folder [alias: tx]
.TP
to\-many
Send a file to many recipients. INCREASED SECURITY RISK!
.PP
Run a subcommand with `\-\-help` to know how it's used.
To send files, use `rwh send <PATH>`.
To receive files, use `rwh receive <CODE>`.
